{"name":"Halcyon Days","hex":"#f7bb73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"halcyon days","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period of calm during the winter, when storms do not occur.","A period of calm, usually in the past and often nostalgic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halcyon_days"}],"entries":[{"title":"Halcyon Days (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Halcyon Days: Interviews with Classic Computer and Video Game Programmers is a digital book edited by James Hague and published in March 1997. The book was originally formatted using HTML and sold via mail order, shipped on a floppy disk by Dadgum Games for US$20. In 2002, Halcyon Days was made freely available on the web. The book continued to be sold by Dr. Dobb's Journal, on a CD-ROM also containing Susan Lammers's Programmers at Work, until Dr. Dobb's shut down at the end of 2014."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Halcyon_Days_%28book%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(book)","wikidata":"Q5641204"},{"title":"Steven Dietz","blocks":[{"text":"Steven Dietz is an American playwright, theatre director, and teacher. Dietz has written over 40 plays and adaptations, including God's Country, Lonely Planet, and Bloomsday. Dietz taught in the MFA Playwriting and Directing programs at the University of Texas at Austin from 2006 to 2018."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_Dietz","wikidata":"Q7614635"},{"title":"Halcyon Days (Ellie Goulding album)","blocks":[{"text":"Halcyon Days is the reissue of English singer Ellie Goulding's second studio album, Halcyon (2012). It was released on 23 August 2013 by Polydor Records. Following the release of Halcyon, Goulding announced that she had plans to repackage the original album, with new songs that focused on electronic music. For the reissue, Goulding recorded 10 new songs and worked with a variety of producers, including Ryan Tedder, Calvin Harris and Greg Kurstin, to create her desired sound."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/HalcyonDaysCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_Days_(Ellie_Goulding_album)","wikidata":"Q17508117"},{"title":"Halcyon (Ellie Goulding album)","blocks":[{"text":"Halcyon is the second studio album by English singer-songwriter Ellie Goulding, released on 5 October 2012, by Polydor Records. It was recorded at multiple studios across the United Kingdom and Canada, including locations in Wales, London, Brighton, and Montreal. She worked with several producers on the album, such as Jim Eliot, Starsmith, Billboard, Justin Parker, and Monsta, in addition to collaborating with artists Tinie Tempah and Calvin Harris."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Ellie_Goulding_-_Halcyon.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halcyon_(Ellie_Goulding_album)","wikidata":"Q3279484"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg/500px-Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg/1280px-Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg/500px-Ellie_Goulding_at_Manchester_Academy_2012_-_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goulding in 2012, performing at the Manchester Academy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.